# Configure Authentication

Use this guide to configure server-side authentication and verify CLI login flows.

## Provider environment variables

Set provider credentials on the Loom server process.

### GitHub OAuth

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID="..."
export LOOM_SERVER_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET="..."
export LOOM_SERVER_GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI="https://YOUR_SERVER/auth/github/callback"
```

### Google OAuth

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="..."
export LOOM_SERVER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="..."
export LOOM_SERVER_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI="https://YOUR_SERVER/auth/google/callback"
```

### Okta OAuth

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_OKTA_DOMAIN="your-org.okta.com"
export LOOM_SERVER_OKTA_CLIENT_ID="..."
export LOOM_SERVER_OKTA_CLIENT_SECRET="..."
export LOOM_SERVER_OKTA_REDIRECT_URI="https://YOUR_SERVER/auth/okta/callback"
```

## Core auth controls

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_AUTH_DEV_MODE=0
export LOOM_SERVER_SIGNUPS_DISABLED=0
```

- `LOOM_SERVER_AUTH_DEV_MODE=1` auto-authenticates requests for development only.
- `LOOM_SERVER_SIGNUPS_DISABLED=1` blocks self-signup and requires provisioning.

<Callout variant="danger" title="Production safety">
	Do not run with `LOOM_SERVER_AUTH_DEV_MODE=1` in production.
</Callout>

## Validate provider availability

The public endpoint below returns enabled providers:

```bash
curl -s https://YOUR_SERVER/auth/providers | jq .
```

## CLI login flow

<Steps>
	<Step title="Authenticate">

```bash
loom --server-url https://YOUR_SERVER login
```

	</Step>
	<Step title="Validate token-dependent command">

```bash
loom --server-url https://YOUR_SERVER weaver ps
```

	</Step>
	<Step title="Logout">

```bash
loom --server-url https://YOUR_SERVER logout
```

	</Step>
</Steps>

## Troubleshooting quick checks

- Redirect URI mismatch: confirm callback URL exactly matches server route.
- Provider not listed in `/auth/providers`: confirm env vars are loaded in the running process.
- Login loop: clear stale cookies/session and retry.
